# Test: a healthy VRRP config produces no vrrp diagnostic (spec-vrrp-5 AC-10).
#
# VALIDATES: `ze doctor` stays silent on a valid vrrp group. This file contains
# exactly ONE command on purpose: reject=stdout:pattern= is matched against the
# WHOLE file's accumulated stdout, not per command, so a `ze explain
# doctor-vrrp-config-invalid` in the same file would print that code and trip the
# reject even though the config is clean (that is precisely how this test first
# failed). Keeping the file to one command is what makes the reject meaningful.
# PREVENTS: a check that cries wolf. The vrrp plugin shares the `interface`
# config root, so it loads on every ze deployment; a diagnostic that fired on
# healthy configs would appear for operators who have never configured VRRP.

tmpfs=vrrp-ok.conf:terminator=EOF_OK
interface {
    backend netlink;
    ethernet eth0 {
        unit 0 {
            ipv4 {
                address [ 192.0.2.251/24 ];
                vrrp {
                    group uplink {
                        vrid 10;
                        virtual-address [ 192.0.2.1 ];
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_OK

# No exit-code assertion, and that is the point. `ze doctor` reports on the
# WHOLE machine, so its exit status carries every check's verdict: checkInterfaces
# (internal/component/doctor/checks_linux.go) emits doctor-iface-missing at ERROR
# severity for a configured ethernet device with no /sys/class/net entry, and
# eth0 above exists on no dev box and on no CI runner. Asserting exit 0 therefore
# asserted the host's NIC inventory, which is why this file was red everywhere.
# The property under test is that the VRRP check stays quiet, so the payload
# assertion below proves doctor ran and produced its JSON and the rejects prove
# no vrrp code is in it.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json vrrp-ok.conf:timeout=60s
expect=stdout:contains=schema-version
reject=stdout:pattern=doctor-vrrp-config-invalid
reject=stdout:pattern=doctor-vrrp-backend-unusable
reject=stdout:pattern=doctor-vrrp-raw-socket
